<<<
Friday &c.) (on Friday &c.) The Puritan way of eating fish is, to eat it Saturday instead of Friday./Can you dine with us Tuesday at 8.0 ?
===
**Friday &c.) (on Friday &c.)** *The Puritan way of eating fish is, to eat it Saturday instead of Friday.*/*Can you dine with us Tuesday at 8.0?*
>>>

<<<
The OED says: ‘The adverbial use of the names of the days of the week is now chiefly U. S. except in collocations like “ next Saturday”, “last Saturday’ ’.
===
The OED says: 'The adverbial use of the names of the days of the week is now chiefly *U. S.* except in collocations like "next Saturday", "last Saturday"'.
>>>

